<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>PHP YARA Vulnerability Scanner v3 – CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (Mac)</Title>
    <Description>&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
.phpScan {font-family:Segoe UI,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#243447;max-width:1000px;margin:8px 12px 20px;}
.phpScan h2 {font-size:20px;color:#183953;margin:0 0 5px;}
.phpScan h3 {font-size:15px;color:#183953;margin:20px 0 8px;padding-bottom:5px;border-bottom:2px solid #dbe5ed;}
.phpScan p {margin:7px 0;}
.phpScan .recommend {background:#edf5fa;border-left:4px solid #28658a;padding:10px 12px;margin:12px 0;}
.phpScan table {width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;margin:8px 0;}
.phpScan th {background:#edf1f5;text-align:left;font-weight:600;}
.phpScan td,.phpScan th {padding:8px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #dce3e9;word-wrap:break-word;}
.phpScan .setting {width:31%;}.phpScan .value {width:18%;}
.phpScan .mode {width:110px;}.phpScan .deep {background:#fff7e7;}
.phpScan .warning {color:#865000;font-weight:bold;}
.phpScan input,.phpScan select,.phpScan button {font-family:inherit;font-size:13px;}
.phpScan input {max-width:95%;}.phpScan input[type=text],.phpScan input:not([type]) {box-sizing:border-box;padding:5px;border:1px solid #9baab7;}
.phpScan select {padding:5px;max-width:100%;}.phpScan input[type=checkbox] {margin-top:3px;}
.phpScan .exclusion input {display:block;width:98%;margin:5px 0;}
.phpScan .hint {color:#516170;font-size:12px;}
.phpScan code {font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;word-wrap:break-word;}
.phpScan .launch {border-top:1px solid #dce3e9;padding-top:12px;margin-top:15px;}
.phpScan button {background:#245b7d;color:white;border:1px solid #194766;padding:8px 16px;cursor:pointer;}
.phpScan button:focus,.phpScan input:focus,.phpScan select:focus {outline:2px solid #438bb7;outline-offset:1px;}
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;div class="phpScan"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;PHP vulnerability scan&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Find PHP runtime versions affected by &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109618&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109619&lt;/strong&gt; on macOS, without running PHP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mac version for team testing.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Use the v3 scanners with the v3 Results Analysis. Scanner and Analysis versions should match. Run a new scan after upgrading to refresh the results.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="recommend"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended: start with Quick Scan and leave the limits at their defaults.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Choose a broader scan only when needed. More coverage increases disk activity and run time.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Document, media, font, ordinary text and selected asset file types are skipped in every scan type, including Deep. Native executables and libraries remain eligible; php-config and php_version.h are retained when PHP build-text detection is enabled. A runtime renamed with an excluded extension can be missed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;1. Choose a scan type&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanPreset"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scan type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/label&gt; &lt;select id="PHPScanPreset" onchange="PhpScan.preset(this.value);"&gt;&lt;option value="quick" selected="selected"&gt;QUICK SCAN (recommended)&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="normal"&gt;NORMAL SCAN&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="deep"&gt;DEEP SCAN&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="custom" disabled="disabled"&gt;CUSTOM (advanced settings)&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="mode" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Scan&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Coverage and tradeoff&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quick&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Standard PHP runtime names in the usual application locations. Fastest; can miss renamed or embedded runtimes.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 10 min search; 10 min content scan; 5 million files; 30 GiB candidate input; 512 MiB per file; 10% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Normal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Also checks renamed/nonstandard binaries, while keeping the usual folder exclusions. Broader runtime coverage; takes longer.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 30 min search; 30 min content scan; 10 million files; 40 GiB candidate input; 512 MiB per file; 10% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr class="deep"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Also includes normally skipped OS/cache/data locations and PHP build text. &lt;span class="warning"&gt;WARNING: This takes much longer and is more likely to hit file and scan limits. Deep already uses the maximum search time, content scan time, file count and total candidate input; it can still hit limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 60 min search; 60 min content scan; 10 million files; 100 GiB candidate input; 1 GiB per file; 25% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Choosing a scan type fills its recommended limits below. Quick and Normal use 512 MiB per file and 10% YARA CPU. Deep uses 1 GiB per file and 25% YARA CPU, with the maximum allowed time, file-count and candidate-input budgets. You can adjust individual settings afterward. Remote storage, cloud placeholders and other permanent exclusions still apply. Build text alone does not prove an installed vulnerable runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;2. Advanced settings (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Changing coverage or a preset limit updates the scan type above; a non-preset combination is shown as Custom. Choosing another scan type resets these settings to its recommended values. Additional directory exclusions are retained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="setting" /&gt;&lt;col class="value" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"&gt;Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Scans other native binary names; leaving this off can miss renamed or custom embedded PHP.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"&gt;Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Includes normally skipped OS and cache folders; remote, cloud-only, snapshot and disk-image exclusions remain.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBuildText"&gt;Include PHP source/build text (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBuildText"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Includes PHP build/header evidence without treating it as an installed runtime.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Time and resource limits&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="setting" /&gt;&lt;col class="value" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPEnumerationSeconds"&gt;File search time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPEnumerationSeconds" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stops searching after this many minutes and marks unfinished coverage as partial. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanSeconds"&gt;Content scan time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPScanSeconds" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Limits YARA content scanning to this many minutes and reports partial results if it times out. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFiles"&gt;Maximum files checked&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFiles" value="5000000" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps files considered during discovery to bound work on unusually large filesystems. (Allowed: 1000 to 10000000.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCandidateGB"&gt;Maximum candidate input (GiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCandidateGB" value="30" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps the combined size of files sent to YARA; exceeding this reports a partial scan. (Allowed: 1 to 100.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFileMB"&gt;Maximum individual file size (MiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFileMB" value="512" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Skips individual files at or above this size; 512 MiB covers normal PHP and large embedded builds. (Allowed: 16 to 2048.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCpuLimit"&gt;YARA CPU setting (%)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCpuLimit" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sets the YARA engine CPU target; this is not a total system CPU guarantee. (Allowed: 1 to 50.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Additional directory exclusions (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class="exclusion"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;label for="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"&gt;Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;input id="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" value="" size="48" maxlength="4096" /&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Skip your chosen folders; leave blank for no additional exclusions. See the examples below.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What is skipped&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/data/*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The named directory and all its subdirectories.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/data/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\folder\&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Only files directly in that directory; subdirectories are still searched.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;*/data/*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;*\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Every matching directory and its subdirectories, wherever found.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Separate entries with commas, without quotes. Use an absolute path or a leading */; * includes path separators and other characters are literal. Windows ignores case; Linux/macOS matching is case-sensitive. Spaces are supported; commas inside a folder name are not. Maximum 32 entries and 4096 UTF-8 bytes. Exclusions apply to every scan type, can hide PHP, and are logged; intentional exclusions do not mark a scan partial.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="launch"&gt;&lt;button onclick="return PhpScan.prepare();"&gt;Configure and Take Action&lt;/button&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Opens the standard Console Take Action dialog, where you select computers. These settings apply only to that action. API/WebUI actions without parameters use Quick defaults; API integrations can supply the same parameters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Reading the results&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="mode" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;An upstream-affected PHP runtime was found. Check vendor patch status and web exposure before deciding remediation.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FALSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;No affected runtime was found within the completed, selected scan scope.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UNKNOWN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;A short reason identifies unavailable results, incomplete coverage or evidence that needs verification. Vendor backports require checking the package advisory.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;Positive findings are retained during a partial scan. BigFix action success includes usable partial results or no PHP found; failure means no new usable result. The four Analysis properties retain the previous finished result while a scan runs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Coverage and requirements&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quick checks php, php-cgi, php-fpm, phpdbg, lsphp, frankenphp, libphp and mod_php name families, including version suffixes and native runtime libraries (.exe/.dll on Windows, .so/.so.N on Linux, .dylib/.so on macOS). PHP core DLLs and server modules are included. Ordinary .php application scripts do not identify an installed runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Legitimate per-user applications remain in scope, including common PHP installations such as Herd, Scoop, Homebrew, MAMP and XAMPP where applicable. OS/recovery trees, caches, backups and personal data are skipped unless broader locations are selected. Network storage, cloud-only files, symlinks, snapshots and scanner/cache data remain excluded. Archives and container images are not unpacked. Meaningful access restrictions and limits produce partial coverage; the scanner does not change system access or privacy settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;macOS: Intel 10.12 or later, or Apple Silicon 11 or later, using stock Bash 3.2, zsh and BSD tools. Minimum OS releases and managed BigFix execution still need team validation. Native payload checks do not replace managed BigFix testing. Uncommon universal-binary formats can produce UNKNOWN/partial results.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Minimum ActionScript syntax: BigFix Client 9.5.7. Use a client supported on the target OS and architecture; this syntax minimum does not establish ARM64 support. The pinned YARA-X engine is delivered by BigFix. No endpoint Python, PHP or compiler is required.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Detailed scan log&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;code&gt;YARA_PHP/scan.log&lt;/code&gt; under the BigFix client state root:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;YARA_PHP/scan.log&lt;/code&gt; under the BigFix client state root (macOS)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;summary.txt supplies the four Analysis properties; scan.lock prevents overlapping scans. Temporary action work is removed after completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Community utility, not HCL-supported patch content. Rule source: &lt;a href="https://github.com/bigfix/Site_Rapid_Response"&gt;Site Rapid Response&lt;/a&gt; (Apache-2.0).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;var phpScanFields = [{"key": "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex", "label": "Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)", "text": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "label": "Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "label": "Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBuildText", "label": "Include PHP source/build text (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPEnumerationSeconds", "label": "File search time (minutes)", "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60}, {"key": "PHPScanSeconds", "label": "Content scan time (minutes)", "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60}, {"key": "PHPMaxFiles", "label": "Maximum files checked", "min": 1000, "max": 10000000}, {"key": "PHPCandidateGB", "label": "Maximum candidate input (GiB)", "min": 1, "max": 100}, {"key": "PHPMaxFileMB", "label": "Maximum individual file size (MiB)", "min": 16, "max": 2048}, {"key": "PHPCpuLimit", "label": "YARA CPU setting (%)", "min": 1, "max": 50}];
var phpScanWindows = false;
/* Console JScript compatible: no JSON dependency, eval, credentials or target selection. */
var PhpScan = (function () {
    function parameters(values) {
        var fields = phpScanFields, selected = {}, index, field, text, number, multiplier, minimum, maximum;
        for (index = 0; index &lt; fields.length; index++) {
            field = fields[index];
            text = String(values[field.key]);
            if (field.text) {
                // Encode UTF-8 bytes, never interpolate a directory into script code.
                if (/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/.test(text)) { throw new Error('Exclusions cannot contain control characters.'); }
                var entries = text.split(','), clean = [], j, entry, encoded, hex = 'x', k, byte;
                for (j = 0; j &lt; entries.length; j++) {
                    entry = entries[j].replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
                    if (!entry) { continue; }
                    var prefix = phpScanWindows ? /^([A-Za-z]:[\\\/]|\*[\\\/])/ : /^(\/|\*\/)/;
                    var relative = phpScanWindows ? /(^|[\\\/])\.{1,2}([\\\/]|$)/ : /(^|\/)\.{1,2}(\/|$)/;
                    if (!prefix.test(entry) || relative.test(entry)) {
                        throw new Error('Use absolute exclusion paths or a leading */; . and .. segments are not allowed.');
                    }
                    clean.push(entry);
                }
                if (clean.length &gt; 32) { throw new Error('Use at most 32 directory exclusions.'); }
                encoded = encodeURIComponent(clean.join(','));
                for (k = 0; k &lt; encoded.length; k++) {
                    if (encoded.charAt(k) === '%') { byte = encoded.substr(k + 1, 2); k += 2; }
                    else { byte = encoded.charCodeAt(k).toString(16); if (byte.length &lt; 2) { byte = '0' + byte; } }
                    hex += byte.toLowerCase();
                }
                if (hex.length &gt; 8193) { throw new Error('Directory exclusions must fit within 4096 UTF-8 bytes.'); }
                selected[field.key] = hex;
                continue;
            }
            if (!/^[0-9]{1,9}$/.test(text)) { throw new Error(field.label + ': enter a whole number.'); }
            number = Number(text);
            multiplier = field.multiplier || 1;
            minimum = Math.ceil(field.min / multiplier);
            maximum = Math.floor(field.max / multiplier);
            if (number &lt; minimum || number &gt; maximum) { throw new Error(field.label + ': use ' + minimum + ' to ' + maximum + '.'); }
            number = number * multiplier;
            selected[field.key] = String(number);
        }
        return selected;
    }
    function prepare() {
        try {
            var values = {}, index, field;
            for (index = 0; index &lt; phpScanFields.length; index++) {
                field = phpScanFields[index];
                values[field.key] = field.checkbox ? (document.getElementById(field.key).checked ? '1' : '0') : document.getElementById(field.key).value;
            }
            var selected = parameters(values);
            if (typeof TakeFixletAction === 'undefined' || typeof Relevance === 'undefined') {
                throw new Error('Open this content in the BigFix Console to use this settings form. API/WebUI launches use defaults unless action parameters are supplied.');
            }
            // These are ordinary, nonsecret action parameters. The Console
            // obtains the current Task's Action1; no XML or script is rebuilt.
            TakeFixletAction(Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), 'Action1', selected);
        } catch (error) { alert('Cannot prepare scan. ' + error.message); }
        return false;
    }
    var presetFields = ["PHPEnumerationSeconds", "PHPScanSeconds", "PHPMaxFiles", "PHPCandidateGB", "PHPMaxFileMB", "PHPCpuLimit", "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "PHPIncludeBuildText"];
    var presetValues = {"quick": [10, 10, 5000000, 30, 512, 10, false, false, false], "normal": [30, 30, 10000000, 40, 512, 10, true, false, false], "deep": [60, 60, 10000000, 100, 1024, 25, true, true, true]};
    function preset(value) {
        var values = presetValues[value], i, field;
        if (!values) { return; }
        for (i = 0; i &lt; presetFields.length; i++) {
            field = document.getElementById(presetFields[i]);
            if (i &lt; 6) { field.value = String(values[i]); }
            else { field.checked = values[i]; }
        }
        document.getElementById('PHPScanPreset').value = value;
    }
    function syncPreset() {
        var modes = ['quick','normal','deep'], mode, values, i, matches, selected = 'custom', field;
        for (mode = 0; mode &lt; modes.length; mode++) {
            values = presetValues[modes[mode]];
            matches = true;
            for (i = 0; i &lt; presetFields.length; i++) {
                field = document.getElementById(presetFields[i]);
                if (i &lt; 6 ? String(field.value) !== String(values[i]) : field.checked !== values[i]) {
                    matches = false;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (matches) { selected = modes[mode]; break; }
        }
        document.getElementById('PHPScanPreset').value = selected;
    }
    return {parameters: parameters, prepare: prepare, preset: preset, syncPreset: syncPreset};
}());
document.body.ontakeaction = function () { return PhpScan.prepare(); };
&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Action scheduling:&lt;/strong&gt; This action stays Running until the scan finishes and can delay other BigFix actions on that system. File search and content scan have separate time limits; their allowed times add together, plus a short shutdown allowance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;API-only PHP extension markers are logged as supporting evidence; they do not by themselves make a scan UNKNOWN.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Standard Homebrew and MacPorts PHP locations are assessed against upstream versions. Custom/vendor patch status and web exposure still require verification.&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
    <Relevance>if version of client &gt;= "9.5.7" then (mac of operating system and ((architecture of operating system = "arm64" and version of operating system &gt;= "11.0") or (architecture of operating system = "x86_64" and version of operating system &gt;= "10.12"))) else false</Relevance>
    <Category>PHP Security Discovery</Category>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to run bounded local PHP discovery.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">begin prefetch block
if {architecture of operating system = "arm64"}
add prefetch item name=yara-x-v1.22.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz sha1=16b30fd7d7613bd0172bc197d785f1143c34f2b9 sha256=79d596da5bf02205de63a1d7844a964daebc7293fa36fcb7da46c3e3c7567229 size=8421133 url=https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/download/v1.22.0/yara-x-v1.22.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
elseif {architecture of operating system = "x86_64"}
add prefetch item name=yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz sha1=560ace0fca8543195a71d52545bef248e92854e4 sha256=d059da4b91c7d7b43f6f50174a7739e3362b51f349f2ba8b33d46e3334bb3300 size=9476144 url=https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/download/v1.22.0/yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
endif
end prefetch block
if {exists parameter "PHPUnixExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
if {not exists parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = "{parameter "PHPUnixExcludeDirectoriesHex"}"
else
continue if {parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = parameter "PHPUnixExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
endif
endif
action uses file encoding UTF-8 NoBOM
if {not exists parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = "x"
endif
continue if {length of parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" &lt;= 8193 and parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = regex "x([0-9A-Fa-f][0-9A-Fa-f])*"}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"}
parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds"}
parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = "600"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPScanSeconds"}
parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = "600"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPScanSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFiles"}
parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = "5000000"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFiles" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &gt;= 1000 and (parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &lt;= 10000000}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCandidateGB"}
parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = "30"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCandidateGB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &lt;= 100}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFileMB"}
parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = "512"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &gt;= 16 and (parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &lt;= 2048}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCpuLimit"}
parameter "PHPCpuLimit" = "10"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCpuLimit" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCpuLimit" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCpuLimit" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCpuLimit" as integer) &lt;= 50}
parameter "output" = "{pathname of parent folder of data folder of client}/YARA_PHP"
// Each attempt owns a separate workspace; interrupted children keep their scan lock.
parameter "work" = "{parameter "output"}/work-{id of action}-{((now - ("01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000" as time)) / microsecond) as integer as string}-{random integer of 2147483647 as string}"
folder create "{parameter "output"}"
folder create "{parameter "work"}"
if {architecture of operating system = "arm64"}
parameter "macArchive" = "yara-x-v1.22.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz"
parameter "macArchiveSha" = "79d596da5bf02205de63a1d7844a964daebc7293fa36fcb7da46c3e3c7567229"
parameter "macEngineSha" = "81f91471e7e786d932e80e8a74e25e0607e0c5305c370ba6238a31133fd2a05f"
elseif {architecture of operating system = "x86_64"}
parameter "macArchive" = "yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz"
parameter "macArchiveSha" = "d059da4b91c7d7b43f6f50174a7739e3362b51f349f2ba8b33d46e3334bb3300"
parameter "macEngineSha" = "aec0e72e7ff4a6efe2fb90419c58f4a539bde31b6804ac24a75f625cf837510c"
endif
delete __createfile
createfile until END_PHP_YARA_0f68f1276f3d50db
/*
  PHP install detection + version, all OSes (Linux ELF, Windows PE, macOS Mach-O).

  Deliberately broad: PHP_Binary_Broad flags anything that looks PHP-related so
  nothing is missed; the other rules carry the exact version string. Run with
  `yara -s` (or `yr scan -s`) to print the matched version text.

  Rules:
    PHP_Runtime_Version     - PHP core runtime; $ver holds the exact version,
                              incl. distro suffix (e.g. 8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    PHP_Windows_VersionInfo - any PE whose version resource says ProductName=PHP
                              (php.exe, php-cgi.exe, php8ts.dll, ext\php_*.dll);
                              $pv holds ProductVersion
    PHP_Binary_Broad        - catch-all: any executable with any PHP marker
    PHP_Build_Artifact      - php-config / php_version.h left by source installs

  No modules are imported so the rules also work in embedded YARA engines
  (osquery, EDRs) that are built without the pe/elf/macho modules.

  See README.md for tested samples and the API number -&gt; branch table.
*/

private rule PHP_Detect_IsExecutable
{{
  condition:
    uint32(0) == 0x464C457F                                 // ELF
    or uint16(0) == 0x5A4D                                  // PE (MZ)
    or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACF   // Mach-O 32/64
    or uint32(0) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(0) == 0xCFFAEDFE   // Mach-O 32/64, byte-swapped
    or uint32(0) == 0xBEBAFECA                              // Mach-O universal (CAFEBABE)
}

rule PHP_Runtime_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "PHP core runtime (CLI/CGI/FPM/mod_php/libphp/php*ts.dll/php8.dll/embedded); $ver = exact version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Compile-time literal "X-Powered-By: PHP/" PHP_VERSION in main/SAPI.c.
    // Present regardless of expose_php. Suffix covers distro builds (8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    // and pre-releases (8.5.0RC1).
    $ver = /X-Powered-By: PHP\/[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}/
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and $ver
}

rule PHP_Windows_VersionInfo
{{
  meta:
    description = "Windows PE with PHP version resource; $pv = ProductVersion (exact version)"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // UTF-16LE "ProductName" &lt;NUL + 0-2 bytes alignment pad&gt; "PHP\0"
    $pname = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $pv = /ProductVersion\x00[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.\-]{{0,20}/ wide
  condition:
    // #pv &gt;= 0 is always true: $pv is only there so -s prints the version
    uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and $pname and #pv &gt;= 0
}

rule PHP_Binary_Broad
{{
  meta:
    description = "Broad catch-all: executable containing any PHP runtime/extension marker"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    $xpb    = "X-Powered-By: PHP/"
    $zend   = "Zend Engine v"
    // ZEND_MODULE_BUILD_ID, e.g. API20220829,NTS / API20250925,TS - also in extensions
    $api    = /API20[0-9]{{6},N?TS/
    $pname  = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $grp    = "The PHP Group" ascii wide
    $ini    = "php.ini"
    $fmt    = "PHP %s (%s)"
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and
    (
      $xpb or $zend or $api or $pname
      or ($grp and ($ini or $fmt))
    )
}

rule PHP_Build_Artifact
{{
  meta:
    description = "php-config script or php_version.h header from a PHP build/install; $v* = version"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    // php-config (installed next to the php binary by `make install` and -dev packages)
    $cfg_ver   = /version="[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}"/
    $cfg_a     = "php_cli_binary="
    $cfg_b     = "--php-binary"
    // main/php_version.h
    $hdr_ver   = /#define PHP_VERSION "[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}"/
    $hdr_a     = "#define PHP_MAJOR_VERSION"
  condition:
    filesize &lt; 64KB and
    (
      ($cfg_ver and $cfg_a and $cfg_b)
      or ($hdr_ver and $hdr_a)
    )
}
END_PHP_YARA_0f68f1276f3d50db
delete "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar"
continue if {sha256 of file "php-detect.yar" of folder (parameter "work") = "0f68f1276f3d50db3dcba06fd1d8089e157fbc8e60bcca49ac1e7b2dde664615"}
delete __createfile
createfile until END_PHP_YARA_5208e234d6eae9fb
#!/bin/bash
# macOS PHP discovery with stock Bash 3.2, BSD utilities and stock zsh modules.
# No Python, jq, GNU tools, compiler or PHP execution required.
# YARA text parsing follows the Apache-2.0 Rapid Response scanner approach.
# Bash 3.2 treats empty arrays as unset under nounset; all inputs below
# are explicitly initialised/validated instead of relying on that option.
set -eo pipefail
export PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin
export LC_ALL=C
umask 077
mac_regex_0='^x([0-9a-fA-F]{{2})*$'
mac_regex_1='^[0-9]{{1,9}$'
mac_regex_2='/\.\.?/'
mac_regex_3='^(php|phpdbg|libphp|mod_php|lsphp|frankenphp)([0-9][0-9.]*([-_][a-z0-9_.-]+)?|[-_][a-z0-9_.-]+)?(ts|nts|apache[0-9_]*)?(\.exe|\.dll|\.dylib|\.so(\.[0-9]+)*)?$'
mac_regex_4='^[0-9][a-z0-9_-]*$'
mac_regex_5='^[0-9]+$'
mac_regex_6='^([0-9]{{1,2})\.([0-9]{{1,2})\.([0-9]{{1,3})(.*)$'
mac_regex_7='^(alpha|beta|RC|dev)[0-9]*$'
mac_regex_8='^(alpha|beta|RC|dev)'
engine= rules= output= archive= engine_sha256= archive_sha256=
enumeration_seconds=600 scan_seconds=600 max_files=5000000 candidate_gb=30
max_file_mb=512 cpu_limit=10 include_build_text=0 include_broader_locations=0 include_nonstandard_names=0
roots=()

valid_utf8() {{
    local text=$1 i byte remaining=0 low=128 high=191
    for ((i=0;i&lt;${{#text};i++)); do
        printf -v byte '%d' "'${{text:i:1}"
        byte=$((byte &amp; 255))
        if ((remaining)); then
            ((byte&gt;=low &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=high)) || return 1
            remaining=$((remaining-1)); low=128; high=191
        elif ((byte&lt;128)); then :
        elif ((byte&gt;=194 &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=223)); then remaining=1
        elif ((byte&gt;=224 &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=239)); then
            remaining=2; ((byte!=224)) || low=160; ((byte!=237)) || high=159
        elif ((byte&gt;=240 &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=244)); then
            remaining=3; ((byte!=240)) || low=144; ((byte!=244)) || high=143
        else return 1; fi
    done
    ((remaining==0))
}
# Shared v3 workspace/path helpers, embedded in both Unix scanners.
cleanup_abandoned_work() {{
    local candidate marker metadata owner mode
    for candidate in "$output"/work-*; do
        [[ -d $candidate &amp;&amp; ! -L $candidate &amp;&amp; $candidate != "$work" ]] || continue
        [[ ${{candidate##*/} =~ ^work-[0-9]+-[0-9]+-[0-9]+$ ]] || continue
        metadata=$(stat -f '%u %Lp' "$candidate" 2&gt;/dev/null) || continue
        read -r owner mode &lt;&lt;&lt;"$metadata"
        [[ $owner = "$EUID" &amp;&amp; $mode =~ ^[0-7]+$ ]] || continue
        (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || continue
        [[ -f $candidate/attempt.started &amp;&amp; ! -L $candidate/attempt.started ]] || continue
        metadata=$(stat -f '%u %Lp' "$candidate/attempt.started" 2&gt;/dev/null) || continue
        read -r owner mode &lt;&lt;&lt;"$metadata"
        [[ $owner = "$EUID" &amp;&amp; $mode =~ ^[0-7]+$ ]] || continue
        (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || continue
        marker=
        IFS= read -r marker &lt;"$candidate/attempt.started" || continue
        [[ $marker = PHP_YARA_WORKSPACE_V3 ]] || continue
        # Only a prior launched-v3 workspace is eligible under the global lock.
        # Unmarked folders may still be in ActionScript preparation: leave them.
        rm -rf -- "$candidate"
    done
    [[ ! -L $work/attempt.started ]] || return 1
    printf 'PHP_YARA_WORKSPACE_V3\n' &gt;"$work/attempt.started"
}

scan_list_path_safe() {{
    [[ $1 != *[[:cntrl:]]* ]] || return 1
    [[ $1 != *[!\ -\~]* ]] || valid_utf8 "$1"
}

stage_candidate() {{
    local available blocks copied
    available=$(df -Pk "$work" 2&gt;/dev/null | awk 'NR&gt;1 {{v=$4} END {{if(v ~ /^[0-9]+$/) print v}') || available=
    blocks=$(((size+1023)/1024))
    if [[ ! $available =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || ((available&lt;blocks+65536)); then
        reasons+=('insufficient free space for unusual-path staging')
        return 1
    fi
    # Non-POSIX Bash ulimit -f uses 1024-byte blocks. Bound growing files too.
    if ! (ulimit -f "$blocks"; timeout -k 2 "$((deadline-SECONDS&gt;0 ? deadline-SECONDS : 1))" cp -p "$path" "$scan_path"); then
        rm -f -- "$scan_path"
        read_errors=$((read_errors+1))
        return 1
    fi
    copied=$(stat -f %z "$scan_path" 2&gt;/dev/null) || copied=
    if [[ $copied != "$size" ]]; then
        rm -f -- "$scan_path"
        read_errors=$((read_errors+1))
        return 1
    fi
}

exclude_directories_hex=x
# macOS adapters, sourced into the generated Bash 3.2-compatible scanner.
# No GNU utilities, Python, PHP, compiler or Homebrew installation is needed.
timeout() {{
    local grace=1 limit
    if [[ $1 = -k ]]; then grace=$2; shift 2; fi
    limit=$1; shift
    /bin/zsh -f "$work/mac-run-bounded.zsh" "$limit" "$grace" "$@"
}

mac_roots() {{
    local line mount filesystem source disposition options data_root=0 images
    [[ ! -d /System/Volumes/Data ]] || data_root=1
    images=$work/disk-images.txt
    if ! timeout -k 1 5 hdiutil info &gt;"$images" 2&gt;"$work/mount.stderr"; then
        reasons+=('disk image inventory unavailable')
        : &gt;"$images"
    fi
    while IFS= read -r line; do
        [[ $line = *' on '* &amp;&amp; $line = *' ('*')' ]] || continue
        source=${{line%% on *}
        mount=${{line#* on }; mount=${{mount% \(*}
        options=${{line##* \(}; options=${{options%)}
        filesystem=${{options%%,*}
        [[ $mount = /* &amp;&amp; $mount != *[[:cntrl:]]* ]] || {{
            reasons+=('unsupported mount path'); continue
        }
        disposition=EXCLUDED
        if [[ $source = /dev/disk* ]]; then
            case "$filesystem" in apfs|hfs|msdos|exfat|ntfs) disposition=SCAN;; *) disposition=UNSUPPORTED;; esac
        fi
        case "$mount" in
            /dev|/net|/home|/System/Volumes/Preboot*|/System/Volumes/VM*|/System/Volumes/Update*|/System/Volumes/Recovery*|/System/Volumes/iSCPreboot*|/System/Volumes/xarts*|/System/Volumes/Hardware*|*/.timemachine/*) disposition=EXCLUDED;;
        esac
        # The APFS Data volume contains user applications. Scanning only / with
        # -xdev can miss it; scanning both logical aliases and Data duplicates it.
        if [[ $mount = / &amp;&amp; $data_root = 1 &amp;&amp; $include_broader_locations = 0 ]]; then disposition=EXCLUDED; fi
        if awk -v device="$source" '$1==device {{found=1} END{{exit !found}' "$images"; then disposition=EXCLUDED; fi
        printf 'Mount: %s | %s | %s\n' "$mount" "$filesystem" "$disposition" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
        case "$disposition" in
            SCAN) roots+=("$mount");;
            UNSUPPORTED) reasons+=('unsupported local filesystem');;
        esac
    done &lt; &lt;(mount)
    # Older macOS releases shipped an Apple PHP runtime on the sealed/system
    # side. It must not disappear just because application Data is separate.
    [[ ! -f /usr/bin/php ]] || roots+=(/usr/bin/php)
}

package_status() {{
    local file=$1 logical answer rc=0 budget index
    for ((index=0;index&lt;${{#package_paths[@]};index++)); do
        if [[ ${{package_paths[index]} = "$file" ]]; then package_state=${{package_states[index]}; return; fi
    done
    logical=${{file#/System/Volumes/Data}
    package_state=unverified
    case "$logical" in
        /System/*|/usr/bin/*) package_state=vendor;;
        /opt/homebrew/Cellar/php/*|/opt/homebrew/Cellar/php@[0-9]*/*|/usr/local/Cellar/php/*|/usr/local/Cellar/php@[0-9]*/*|/opt/local/bin/php*|/opt/local/sbin/php*|/opt/local/lib/php*|/opt/local/apache*/modules/*php*)
            # Standard package-manager PHP is assessed against upstream versions.
            # This does not establish the patch status of a custom build.
            package_state=upstream;;
        *)
            budget=$((package_deadline-SECONDS)); ((budget&lt;=2)) || budget=2
            if ((budget&gt;=1)); then
                answer=$(timeout -k 1 "$budget" pkgutil --file-info "$logical" 2&gt;&amp;1 | head -c 8192) || rc=$?
                if ((rc==0)); then
                    # A successful query can describe a path without any owning
                    # receipt. Require pkgid evidence before calling it managed;
                    # unknown output remains unverified rather than guessing.
                    case "$answer" in
                        pkgid:\ *|*$'\npkgid: '*) package_state=vendor;;
                        volume:\ *$'\npath: '*) package_state=unowned;;
                    esac
                elif ((rc==1)) &amp;&amp; [[ $answer = *'No receipt for'* ]]; then package_state=unowned; fi
            fi;;
    esac
    package_paths+=("$file"); package_states+=("$package_state")
}

while (($#)); do
    (($# &gt;= 2)) || {{ echo 'Missing argument' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    case "$1" in
        --engine) engine=$2;; --engine-sha256) engine_sha256=$2;; --rules) rules=$2;; --output) output=$2;;
        --archive) archive=$2;; --archive-sha256) archive_sha256=$2;; --root) roots+=("$2");;
        --enumeration-seconds) enumeration_seconds=$2;; --scan-seconds) scan_seconds=$2;;
        --max-files) max_files=$2;; --candidate-gb) candidate_gb=$2;; --max-file-mb) max_file_mb=$2;;
        --cpu-limit) cpu_limit=$2;; --include-build-text) include_build_text=$2;;
        --include-broader-locations) include_broader_locations=$2;; --include-nonstandard-names) include_nonstandard_names=$2;;
        --exclude-directories-hex) exclude_directories_hex=$2;;
        *) echo 'Unknown argument' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2;;
    esac
    shift 2
done
for name in enumeration_seconds scan_seconds max_files candidate_gb max_file_mb cpu_limit include_build_text include_broader_locations include_nonstandard_names; do
    [[ ${{!name} =~ $mac_regex_1 ]] || {{ echo "Invalid $name" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
done
((enumeration_seconds&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; enumeration_seconds&lt;=3600 &amp;&amp; scan_seconds&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; scan_seconds&lt;=3600 &amp;&amp; max_files&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; max_files&lt;=10000000 &amp;&amp; candidate_gb&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; candidate_gb&lt;=100 &amp;&amp; max_file_mb&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; max_file_mb&lt;=2048 &amp;&amp; cpu_limit&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; cpu_limit&lt;=99 &amp;&amp; include_build_text&lt;=1 &amp;&amp; include_broader_locations&lt;=1 &amp;&amp; include_nonstandard_names&lt;=1)) || {{ echo 'Scan setting outside its allowed range' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
[[ $output = /* &amp;&amp; $engine = /* &amp;&amp; $rules = /* ]] || {{ echo 'Engine, rule and output paths must be absolute' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
missing=()
for command in df find stat od awk sort shasum tar gzip date mkdir mv chmod dirname mkfifo cp nice cat head tr rm zsh pkgutil hdiutil mount; do
    command -v "$command" &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || missing+=("$command")
done
((${{#missing[@]}==0)) || {{ printf 'Missing required utilities: %s\n' "${{missing[*]}" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
# Reject symlink output ancestors and insecure output ownership. Never change
# permissions on an unrelated directory and never follow an output redirect.
current=$output
while [[ $current != / ]]; do [[ ! -L $current ]] || {{ echo 'Symlink output ancestor rejected' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }; current=${{current%/*}; [[ -n $current ]] || current=/; done
mkdir -p -- "$output"
[[ $(stat -f %u "$output") = "$EUID" ]] || {{ echo 'Output directory ownership mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
mode=$(stat -f %Lp "$output"); (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || {{ echo 'Output directory is writable by another account' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
for leaf in scan.lock scan.log scan.log.new summary.txt summary.txt.new; do [[ ! -L $output/$leaf ]] || {{ echo "Symlink output file rejected: $leaf" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }; done
# The pinned mac-lock.zsh launcher execs this process while retaining its
# kernel advisory lock. Never reopen/close the locked inode in this process.
[[ ${{PHP_SCAN_LOCK_HELD_PID-} = "$$" ]] || {{ echo 'Use the locked macOS launcher' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
work=$(dirname -- "$engine")
[[ -d $work &amp;&amp; ! -L $work &amp;&amp; $(stat -f %u "$work") = "$EUID" ]] || {{ echo 'Unsafe or missing scan workspace' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
mode=$(stat -f %Lp "$work"); (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || {{ echo 'Scan workspace is writable by another account' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
started=$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC'); start_seconds=$SECONDS
# Persistent header worker: one process per scan instead of several per file.
# The request/response FIFOs are private attempt-owned objects. Opening both
# ends in the parent avoids startup/EOF races; read -t applies to the FIFO.
header_pid=
stop_header_worker() {{
    if [[ -n $header_pid ]]; then
        kill -KILL "$header_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :
        wait "$header_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :
        header_pid=
    fi
    exec 6&gt;&amp;- 7&gt;&amp;-
}
start_header_worker() {{
    local leaf
    for leaf in header-request.pipe header-response.pipe; do
        [[ ! -L $work/$leaf ]] || return 1
        if [[ -e $work/$leaf ]]; then [[ -p $work/$leaf ]] || return 1; rm -f -- "$work/$leaf"; fi
        mkfifo -- "$work/$leaf" || return 1
    done
    exec 7&lt;&gt;"$work/header-request.pipe" 6&lt;&gt;"$work/header-response.pipe"
    /bin/bash "$work/mac-read-header.sh" "$work/header-request.pipe" "$work/header-response.pipe" &amp;
    header_pid=$!
}
read_header() {{
    local reply expected_size=$2 hexadecimal_pattern='^[0-9a-f]+$'
    local expected_length=$(( (expected_size&lt;20 ? expected_size : 20)*2 ))
    header=
    if [[ -z $header_pid ]]; then start_header_worker || return 1; fi
    if printf '%s\0' "$1" &gt;&amp;7 &amp;&amp; IFS= read -r -d '' -t 2 reply &lt;&amp;6; then
        if [[ $reply = OK:* ]]; then
            header=${{reply#OK:}
            if [[ $header =~ $hexadecimal_pattern ]] &amp;&amp; ((${{#header}==expected_length)); then return 0; fi
        fi
    fi
    # Only this read-only attempt-owned worker is terminated, never an app.
    stop_header_worker
    return 1
}

finished=0 find_pid= scan_pid=
failure() {{
    result=$?
    trap - EXIT
    stop_header_worker
    if [[ -n $find_pid ]]; then kill "$find_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; wait "$find_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; fi
    if [[ -n $scan_pid ]]; then kill "$scan_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; wait "$scan_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; fi
    if (( !finished )); then
        printf '\nScan failed (exit %s); previous finished results retained.\n' "$result" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
        if [[ -f $output/summary.txt ]]; then
            awk '/^LAST_SCAN=/{{sub(/ \(Last attempt failed.*/, ""); print $0 " (Last attempt failed; see scan.log)"; next} {{print}' "$output/summary.txt" &gt;"$output/summary.txt.new"
        else printf 'RESULT_FORMAT=2\nDETECTED=UNKNOWN\nLAST_SCAN=NO SCAN (Last attempt failed; see scan.log)\nDURATION=NO SCAN\n' &gt;"$output/summary.txt.new"; fi
        mv -f -- "$output/summary.txt.new" "$output/summary.txt"
    fi
    exit "$result"
}
trap failure EXIT
trap 'exit 130' INT TERM
printf 'PHP scan started: %s\nStandard names: %s; build text: %s; broader locations: %s\n' "$started" "$((1-include_nonstandard_names))" "$include_build_text" "$include_broader_locations" &gt;"$output/scan.log"
exec 2&gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
cleanup_abandoned_work
# Decode only validated byte pairs. Paths are never shell code, printf formats or
# evaluated expressions. BSD find gets quoted regex arguments with literal syntax
# escaped; only '*' is a wildcard. Directory pruning happens before any file read.
[[ ${{#exclude_directories_hex} -le 8193 &amp;&amp; $exclude_directories_hex =~ $mac_regex_0 ]] || {{ echo 'Invalid encoded exclusions' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
exclusion_text=
for ((i=1;i&lt;${{#exclude_directories_hex};i+=2)); do
    pair=${{exclude_directories_hex:i:2}
    [[ $pair != 00 ]] || {{ echo 'NUL in exclusions' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    printf -v character '%b' "\\x$pair"; exclusion_text+=$character
done
[[ $exclusion_text != *[[:cntrl:]]* ]] || {{ echo 'Control character in exclusions' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
custom_trees=(); custom_direct=(); custom_patterns=()
IFS=',' read -r -a exclusion_entries &lt;&lt;&lt;"$exclusion_text"
for pattern in "${{exclusion_entries[@]}"; do
    pattern="${{pattern#"${{pattern%%[![:space:]]*}"}"; pattern="${{pattern%"${{pattern##*[![:space:]]}"}"
    [[ -n $pattern ]] || continue
    ((${{#custom_patterns[@]}&lt;32)) || {{ echo 'At most 32 exclusions allowed' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    [[ $pattern = /* || $pattern = \*/* ]] || {{ echo 'Unix exclusions need an absolute path or leading */' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    [[ ! /$pattern/ =~ $mac_regex_2 ]] || {{ echo 'Relative path segments are not allowed' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    while [[ $pattern = *//* ]]; do pattern=${{pattern//\/\//\/}; done
    while [[ $pattern = *\*\** ]]; do pattern=${{pattern//\*\*/\*}; done
    custom_patterns+=("$pattern")
    recursive=0; basis=$pattern
    if [[ $basis = */\* ]]; then recursive=1; basis=${{basis%/\*}; fi
    while [[ $basis = */ ]]; do basis=${{basis%/}; done
    expression=
    for ((i=0;i&lt;${{#basis};i++)); do
        character=${{basis:i:1}
        case "$character" in
            '*') expression+='.*';;
            '.'|'['|']'|'('|')'|'{{'|'}'|'+'|'?'|'^'|'$'|'|'|'\') expression+="\\$character";;
            *) expression+=$character;;
        esac
    done
    if ((recursive)); then custom_trees+=("$expression(/.*)?"); else custom_direct+=("$expression/[^/]+"); fi
    printf 'Custom directory exclusion: %s\n' "$pattern" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
done
hash() {{ shasum -a 256 "$1" | awk '{{print $1}'; }
[[ $(hash "$rules") = 0f68f1276f3d50db3dcba06fd1d8089e157fbc8e60bcca49ac1e7b2dde664615 ]] || {{ echo 'Rule hash mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
if [[ ! -f $engine ]]; then
    [[ -f $archive &amp;&amp; $(hash "$archive") = "$archive_sha256" ]] || {{ echo 'Archive hash mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    # Extract only the pinned executable to a controlled filename; no archive paths.
    tar -xOzf "$archive" yr &gt;"$engine"
    chmod 700 "$engine"
fi
[[ $(hash "$engine") = "$engine_sha256" ]] || {{ echo 'Engine hash mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
prune=(/dev /net /home /Volumes/TimeMachine /private/var/vm "$output")
if [[ ${{output##*/} = YARA_PHP ]]; then prune+=("${{output%/*}/__BESData"); fi
if (( !include_broader_locations )); then
    prune+=(/System /bin /sbin /usr/bin /usr/sbin /usr/lib /usr/share /Library/Apple /private/var/log /private/var/cache /private/var/folders)
fi
# Include physical APFS Data paths for exclusions expressed using logical paths.
for directory in "${{prune[@]}"; do
    [[ $directory = /System/Volumes/Data/* ]] || prune+=("/System/Volumes/Data$directory")
done
reasons=()
if ((${{#roots[@]}==0)); then mac_roots; fi
((${{#roots[@]})) || {{ echo 'No supported local filesystem found' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
name_expression=( '(' -iname 'php*' -o -iname 'libphp*' -o -iname 'mod_php*' -o -iname 'lsphp*' -o -iname 'frankenphp*' ')' )
((include_nonstandard_names)) &amp;&amp; name_expression=()
prune_expression=( '(' -type d '(' -false )
for directory in "${{prune[@]}"; do prune_expression+=( -o -path "$directory" ); done
prune_expression+=( -o -path '*/Library/CloudStorage' -o -path '*/Library/Mobile Documents' -o -path '*/Library/Containers/com.docker.docker' -o -path '*/.Trash' -o -path '*/.Trashes' -o -path '*/.Spotlight-V100' -o -path '*/.fseventsd' )
for expression in "${{custom_trees[@]}"; do prune_expression+=( -o -regex "$expression" -o -regex "/System/Volumes/Data$expression" ); done
if ((!include_broader_locations)); then prune_expression+=( -o -path '*/Library/Caches' -o -path '*/Library/Logs' -o -path '*/.cache' -o -path '*/.npm/_cacache' -o -path '*/.nuget/packages' ); fi
prune_expression+=( ')' ')' -prune -o )
